build/
.venv/
# Also without the slash, for the same reason /tools carries one in the
# top-level file: a git worktree does not inherit the virtualenv, so it
# gets symlinked here, and a symlink is a file — `.venv/` would not
# match it and an absolute path out of someone's home directory would be
# one `git add -A` away from a public repository.
/.venv
hw/sim/sim_build*/
hw/sim/results.xml
# The verilog-ethernet submodule was deregistered on 2026-08-12, but the
# checkout survives in every working tree that predates it, and it is a
# nested git repository: `git add -A` stages it as a gitlink with no
# .gitmodules to resolve, which a clone cannot fetch. Deleting the
# directory is the operator's call, not git's.
hw/vendor/verilog-ethernet/
__pycache__/
*.fst
*.vcd
